Summary: The main objective of the AF STTR effort is to develop HALAR-L, an innovative
electromagnetic optical disruption solution designed to effectively deny intelligence collection and
intrusion by small Unmanned Aerial Systems (sUAS) within restricted areas. This system employs a
multi-beam laser approach to Warn, Dazzle and Deny sUAS sensors. HALAR-L integrates with a
sophisticated detect and track unit, enabling both standalone and mobile platform deployment for
maximum operational flexibility. Critically, the system''s architecture is scalable, accommodating both
low-power, eye-safe lasers for urban operations and high-power lasers for more robust protection
against advanced sUAS threats. A key objective of the HALAR-L program is to minimize size, weight,
power (SWaP), complexity, and cost per unit. This focus on SWaP-C reduction will ensure HALAR-L''s
versatility and adaptability across diverse operational environments, including complex urban settings
with civilian infrastructure and air traffic considerations with an effort to minimize collateral effects.
Title: “Enhanced OPSEC for Air Force Mission Functions Utilizing a Networkable Nonlethal Directed
Energy Solution” AF STTR Phase I (5/5/2023- 8/7/2023) RI Partner- The Ohio State University
Summary: Immobileyes HALAR solutions, in conjunction with computer vision systems, can provide an
immediate non-lethal deterrent and counter-intelligence capability in areas deemed sensitive. The system
distracts and disrupts visual perception in the affected area. The same system can also be used to mitigate
the threat of active shooters or other engagements which would benefit from disrupting visual acuity. The
solutions utilize 100% eye-safe certified LEDs which are programmable to allow for patterns of effect.
Targeted End Users – Any Security Forces organization tasked with controlling sensitive areas and/or
information. Defenders with responsibility for base security and access denial.
Title: “Throwable Portable HALAR Visual Disrupter for Air Force Rapid Tactical & Security Operations”
AF STTR Phase I (5/5/2023- 8/7/2023) RI - Kent State University
Summary: HALAR is an innovative patented platform technology representing an innovative leap
forward in optical distraction, disorientation, diversion, and dazzling non-lethal threat mitigation
solutions. The HALAR solutions represent the first non-laser eye-safe non-lethal system designed for
Military Security Forces and Law Enforcement missions. The HALAR utilizes high-power multi-color
LEDs that are programable allowing them to flash in a particular sequence known to cause physiological
effects such as: dizziness, disorientation, glare, and dazzle/flash blind effects.
Title: “Small UAS Detection and Classification for Rapid Multiple C-UAS Operations using a Novel
Multi-Wavelength Directed Energy Technology” AF STTR Phase I (5/5/2023- 8/7/2023) RI - UT
Summary: HALAR Laser Storm is a patented, scalable, and programmable laser-emitting device
capable of projecting a “shower” of multiple wavelength laser beams adapted to overwhelm multiple
sensors. It offers a novel approach in the use of multiple laser lights as a force multiplier for counter
surveillance, counter unmanned aerial systems, and other value-added Air Force applications. In this
project, Immobileyes will to test the feasibility of adapting its technology to “Track and Blind” multiple
UAVs in a low C-SwaP system.
