Phase II will focus on delivering a prototype and demonstrating operational value at a military base,
which will provide the validation necessary to support Phase III transition funding.
7. Key Personnel
Atossa Alavi, CEO (PI – US Citizen) is an entrepreneur, intellectual property (IP) lawyer, and
technology executive with over 15 years of experience at the intersection of law, business strategy, and
advanced product development. As Chief Executive Officer of Immobileyes, she has successfully raised
$2 million in non-dilutive SBIR funding from the U.S. Air Force, assembled and led cross-disciplinary
engineering teams, and driven the development, fielding, and commercialization of novel non-lethal
optical disruptor technologies for law enforcement and Air Force Security Forces. She has also served as
Chief Counsel of AlphaMicron, guiding IP strategy and portfolio development, negotiating joint
development and licensing agreements, and managing corporate legal functions that supported the
transition of adaptive liquid crystal technologies into Army eyewear, automotive, motorsports, and
architectural applications. She is a named inventor on three patents for HALAR optical disruption
technology and has built extensive partnerships with DoD, DHS, and commercial stakeholders to advance
non-lethal defense and security solutions.
Ms. Alavi has made significant contributions as an educator and community leader. She served as an
Adjunct Professor at Case Western Reserve University School of Law. Before entering law, she trained
and practiced in neuroscience and oral surgery in the UK, publishing peer-reviewed research on
neuroreceptors and serving as Assistant Professor at the Eastman Dental Institute, University of London.
She holds a Juris Doctor (2003) from Case Western Reserve University, an MPhil in Neuroscience (2000)
from University College London, and a BDS and MSc in Endodontics from the University of London.
Bahman Taheri, CTO (US Citizen, Secret Clearance) is the CEO of AlphaMicron and CTO of
Immobileyes. With over 25 years of experience in optics and materials science, he has led cross-
disciplinary teams that transitioned advanced electro-optic and liquid crystal innovations from research to
fielded systems. Under his leadership, AlphaMicron developed the world’s first switchable-tint liquid
crystal eyewear, meeting U.S. Army protective eyewear standards and is currently the only electronically
switchable eyewear on the Approved Protective Eyewear List (APEL). Under his leadership, the team has
delivered light-management solutions for defense, automotive, and commercial partners. He has managed
multimillion-dollar R&D programs with the Air Force, Navy, Army, DOE, NSF, and Fortune 500
companies.
Dr. Taheri is an inventor on more than 90 patents and author of over 70 peer-reviewed scientific articles,
as well as a technical book on liquid crystal optics. His innovations include the first demonstration of
continuous-wave lasing in liquid crystals, development of fast-switching electro-optic systems for laser
and nuclear flash protection, and commercialization of photochromic-dichroic lens technologies. He has
received multiple innovation awards, served as a frequent invited speaker at defense and industry
conferences, and has extensive experience in transitioning advanced optical technologies to DoD and
dual-use markets. He earned his PhD and MS in Physics from Oklahoma State University and a BS in
Physics from Cal Poly San Luis Obispo.
