  VALUES ('9455652f-b940-4d60-b5a5-ace862b15006'::uuid, tid, 'primitive', 'p3 · Signature:
Printed Name Signature Title Business Name ', 'Signature:
Printed Name Signature Title Business Name Date
Atossa Alavi Atossa M Alavi CEO Immobileyes Inc. 10/21/2020
Audit Information
Summary:
Has your Firm ever had a DCAA review?NO
VOL I - Proposal Summary
Summary:
Proposed Base Duration (in months): 6
Option 1 Duration (in months): 6
Technical Abstract:
This Phase I effort evaluates the feasibility of adapting the current IMMOBILEYES laser system into a light-based, non-lethal
Warn/Dazzle Gate Defense for perimeter security. Addressing the need for layered deterrence at military access points, the
proposed LEOPARD system (Light-based Electro-Optic Perimeter Active Response Defense) employs adaptive laser responses
across three zones: Warn, Dazzle, and Deny. Utilizing multiple wavelengths (green and blue), beam divergence control, and
laser splitting, LEOPARD maximizes effectiveness while maintaining eye safety. This approach allows for scalable, non-kinetic
escalation against personnel or vehicles, with visible warnings and temporary visual disruption tailored to threat intent and
proximity. Compared to conventional dazzlers, the system achieves wider area coverage, greater effective range, and reduced
power requirements—demonstrating a 40× reduction in laser power while enhancing safety and performance.
Anticipated Benefits/Potential Commercial Applications of the Research or Development:
The LEOPARD system offers a non-lethal, adaptive deterrence solution designed to enhance security at military bases, forward
operating locations, and critical homeland infrastructure. By providing a visible warning and scalable visual disruption while
maintaining strict eye-safety, it addresses a key capability gap at access control points—reducing reliance on barriers or lethal
force. Potential applications include fixed site defense, expeditionary perimeter security, and protection of airfields, ports, and
energy facilities. The system’s low-power, beam-splitting laser architecture supports flexible deployment with minimal
logistical burden. LEOPARD’s ability to safely and effectively deter personnel or vehicles at range enables rapid threat', '[{"id":"5a09068e-f8fb-46d8-b329-0debbf8b02d1","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"Signature:\nPrinted Name Signature Title Business Name Date\nAtossa Alavi Atossa M Alavi CEO Immobileyes Inc. 10/21/2020\nAudit Information\nSummary:\nHas your Firm ever had a DCAA review?NO\nVOL I - Proposal Summary\nSummary:\nProposed Base Duration (in months): 6\nOption 1 Duration (in months): 6\nTechnical Abstract:\nThis Phase I effort evaluates the feasibility of adapting the current IMMOBILEYES laser system into a light-based, non-lethal\nWarn/Dazzle Gate Defense for perimeter security. Addressing the need for layered deterrence at military access points, the\nproposed LEOPARD system (Light-based Electro-Optic Perimeter Active Response Defense) employs adaptive laser responses\nacross three zones: Warn, Dazzle, and Deny. Utilizing multiple wavelengths (green and blue), beam divergence control, and\nlaser splitting, LEOPARD maximizes effectiveness while maintaining eye safety. This approach allows for scalable, non-kinetic\nescalation against personnel or vehicles, with visible warnings and temporary visual disruption tailored to threat intent and\nproximity. Compared to conventional dazzlers, the system achieves wider area coverage, greater effective range, and reduced\npower requirements—demonstrating a 40× reduction in laser power while enhancing safety and performance.\nAnticipated Benefits/Potential Commercial Applications of the Research or Development:\nThe LEOPARD system offers a non-lethal, adaptive deterrence solution designed to enhance security at military bases, forward\noperating locations, and critical homeland infrastructure. By providing a visible warning and scalable visual disruption while\nmaintaining strict eye-safety, it addresses a key capability gap at access control points—reducing reliance on barriers or lethal\nforce. Potential applications include fixed site defense, expeditionary perimeter security, and protection of airfields, ports, and\nenergy facilities. The system’s low-power, beam-splitting laser architecture supports flexible deployment with minimal\nlogistical burden. LEOPARD’s ability to safely and effectively deter personnel or vehicles at range enables rapid threat"},"history":[],"provenance":{"source":"imported"},"library_eligible":true}]'::jsonb, NULL, 280, 2121, '{}'::jsonb, 'approved', 0.5, 'pending', 0.5, 0, 'upload', 'f5d07400-ac40-491e-9a0e-70b7e76d79f6'::uuid, NULL, NULL, '686842de-ae88-44ac-b724-8e550f079e3e'::uuid, 'tenant', '2026-08-18T22:42:54.071Z'::timestamptz, '2026-08-18T22:42:54.071Z'::timestamptz, 'admin', uid, '[{"blockIds":["b3"],"sourceAtomId":"f4eab274-3a1e-4d95-b6ac-6d10f53147e8"}]'::jsonb, NULL)
