since protective lenses cannot block both colors simultaneously.
At the core of the system is the patented HALAR system, developed by Immobileyes under an Air Force
STTR (now TACFI) contract with the support of Tinker Af Security Forces Squadron, delivering a low-
SWAP-C counter UAV solution that includes multiple lasers integrated into an EO/IR camera for
detection & tracking. The system enables a scalable, low-collateral defeat Warn and Dazzle response
prior to kinetic engagement, desirable for a base in an urban setting.
In addition to the 2 lasers emitters, the system employs a laser range finder
for precise ranging and can include any number of fixed cameras to
provide up to 360o surveillance at any point of entry.
C: Innovation / Differentiation from conventional dazzlers
I. “SHOT GUN approach:
The Immobileyes laser system is uniquely capable of switching from a
single laser to a cluster of low-divergence laser beams (or beamlets).
The number of beamlets and the projected pattern is highly adaptable and
can be designed to cover a specified area at various distances. The low
divergence of each beamlet means it can deliver the required intensity at
greater distances. Using both diverging optics and splitting optics makes
the system superior to conventional dazzlers. Beam splitting/shaping is highly adaptable and results in:
(1) increased effective range,
(2) wider area cover,
(3) reduced laser power,
(4) increased eye-safety over a longer range,
(5) reduced SWAP-C of the system,
(6) an adaptable system that can provide
different responses.
For example, using the DSLA as comparison, a cluster of low divergence beams from a 250mW laser can
deliver the same intensity over a 3m spot at 300m as compared to the DSLA’s 10W laser. This is an X40
reduction in power.
Low SWAP-C Laser +
EO/IR detection &
tracking C-sUAS
360 Fixed
