Air Force applications. In this\nproject, Immobileyes will to test the feasibility of adapting its technology to “Track and Blind” multiple\nUAVs in a low C-SwaP system.\nTitle: “Intelligent Air Laser System for Mission Support w/ Multi UAVs Equipped with Laser Beams”\nAF STTR Phase I (4/24/2021-7/23/2021) RI: Kent State University\nUnder this project, Immobileyes evaluated developing a rapidly deployable UAS-mounted non-lethal\nIntelligent Air Laser (AIL) System to provide USAF Security Forces with a rapid & safe technology\ncapable of dazzling, distracting, and disrupting hostile threats utilizing hundreds of multicolored moving"},"history":[],"provenance":{"source":"imported"},"library_eligible":true}]'::jsonb, NULL, 610, 4382, '{}'::jsonb, 'approved', 0.5, 'pending', 0.5, 0, 'upload', 'f5d07400-ac40-491e-9a0e-70b7e76d79f6'::uuid, NULL, NULL, '686842de-ae88-44ac-b724-8e550f079e3e'::uuid, 'tenant', '2026-08-18T22:42:54.259Z'::timestamptz, '2026-08-18T22:42:54.259Z'::timestamptz, 'admin', uid, '[{"blockIds":["b13"],"sourceAtomId":"c4b9486f-79dd-4135-9ad8-3541e505e828"}]'::jsonb, NULL)
