  VALUES ('7fe3e29f-e00e-4070-9073-068774d576d2'::uuid, tid, 'primitive', 'p7 · Introduction and Summary: Counter-UAS and Defeat of Dr', 'Introduction and Summary: Counter-UAS and Defeat of Drone Surveillance Using Directed Energy System
Company Name: Immobileyes
Proposal Number: FX235-CSO1-0859 Topic: USAF X23.5_CSO
Identified and Engaged USAF End-Users: AF Security Forces Center – AF Installation and Mission Support Center
1
Topic: X23.5_CSO 	Proposal Number: FX235-CSO1-0859
“Base-Wide Counter-UAS and Defeat of Drone Surveillance Utilizing Innovative Directed Energy System”
Technical Abstract: Immobileyes has invented an innovative, patented, programmable, scalable directed energy (LED and
Laser) disruption and dazzling system called HALAR. The solution revolutionizes the application of light as a non-lethal force
multiplier for security, OPSEC, counter surveillance, counter unmanned aerial systems, and a litany of other value-added Air
Force applications. For this project, Immobileyes will work with key Air Force stakeholders to evaluate the feasibility of
adapting Immobileyes’ HALAR Hive dazzler solution to neutralize surveillance threats posed by the emergence of drones.
Overview: In Phase I, Immobileyes will work with our identified key Air Force stakeholders, led by the AFSFC (Letter of
Support) and AFIMSC, to evaluate the feasibility of utilizing the Immobileyes HALAR Hive solution for base-wide
counter UAS and drone surveillance defeat. When successful feasibility is demonstrated, Immobileyes will work with the
Air Force end-users and Phase II partners to develop a Work Plan for a Phase II effort which culminates in a fieldable and
commercially available solution for integration into Air Force base security and OPSEC systems.
Technical Merit: The Immobileyes HALAR solutions are based on over two decades of research by known thought
leaders in the fields of physics, optics, and electronics. The HALAR solutions represent the first transformative
improvements to known existing light and dazzler technologies in the last two decades. The Hive is programable and
scalable to address various AF security operational parameters.
Team: The Immobileyes is comprised of serial entrepreneurs, optics and electronics experts, product developers,
engineering, legal, and and electronics manufacturing with a long history of successfully developing and transitioning
invention to commercial product. 	Adaptation of Immobileyes’ existing solution significantly de-risks the project.
Commercialization : The founders of Immobileyes have successfully commercialized numerous electro-optical solutions
for various markets over the last several decades. With over 90 granted patents and a proven track record of
commercialization, the Immobileyes team is confident in the commercial potential of this solution.', '[{"id":"821688eb-2f9b-446b-8a23-b7ff8fe6391a","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"Introduction and Summary: Counter-UAS and Defeat of Drone Surveillance Using Directed Energy System\nCompany Name: Immobileyes\nProposal Number: FX235-CSO1-0859 Topic: USAF X23.5_CSO\nIdentified and Engaged USAF End-Users: AF Security Forces Center – AF Installation and Mission Support Center\n1\nTopic: X23.5_CSO \tProposal Number: FX235-CSO1-0859\n“Base-Wide Counter-UAS and Defeat of Drone Surveillance Utilizing Innovative Directed Energy System”\nTechnical Abstract: Immobileyes has invented an innovative, patented, programmable, scalable directed energy (LED and\nLaser) disruption and dazzling system called HALAR. The solution revolutionizes the application of light as a non-lethal force\nmultiplier for security, OPSEC, counter surveillance, counter unmanned aerial systems, and a litany of other value-added Air\nForce applications. For this project, Immobileyes will work with key Air Force stakeholders to evaluate the feasibility of\nadapting Immobileyes’ HALAR Hive dazzler solution to neutralize surveillance threats posed by the emergence of drones.\nOverview: In Phase I, Immobileyes will work with our identified key Air Force stakeholders, led by the AFSFC (Letter of\nSupport) and AFIMSC, to evaluate the feasibility of utilizing the Immobileyes HALAR Hive solution for base-wide\ncounter UAS and drone surveillance defeat. When successful feasibility is demonstrated, Immobileyes will work with the\nAir Force end-users and Phase II partners to develop a Work Plan for a Phase II effort which culminates in a fieldable and\ncommercially available solution for integration into Air Force base security and OPSEC systems.\nTechnical Merit: The Immobileyes HALAR solutions are based on over two decades of research by known thought\nleaders in the fields of physics, optics, and electronics. The HALAR solutions represent the first transformative\nimprovements to known existing light and dazzler technologies in the last two decades. The Hive is programable and\nscalable to address various AF security operational parameters.\nTeam: The Immobileyes is comprised of serial entrepreneurs, optics and electronics experts, product developers,\nengineering, legal, and and electronics manufacturing with a long history of successfully developing and transitioning\ninvention to commercial product. \tAdaptation of Immobileyes’ existing solution significantly de-risks the project.\nCommercialization : The founders of Immobileyes have successfully commercialized numerous electro-optical solutions\nfor various markets over the last several decades. With over 90 granted patents and a proven track record of\ncommercialization, the Immobileyes team is confident in the commercial potential of this solution."},"history":[],"provenance":{"source":"imported"},"library_eligible":true}]'::jsonb, NULL, 372, 2697, '{}'::jsonb, 'approved', 0.5, 'pending', 0.5, 0, 'upload', '31c0c32b-a7c5-47fc-817b-55a3b84f960f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, '686842de-ae88-44ac-b724-8e550f079e3e'::uuid, 'tenant', '2026-08-18T22:42:56.398Z'::timestamptz, '2026-08-18T22:42:56.398Z'::timestamptz, 'admin', uid, '[{"blockIds":["b7"],"sourceAtomId":"61cb1be6-93f1-4af6-9561-8b8fb5b5e554"}]'::jsonb, NULL)
  ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

