  VALUES ('1ac91f33-f223-47f4-a530-02d858ff0761'::uuid, tid, 'primitive', 'p31 · Summary of Project and Contact Information
25
For this', 'Summary of Project and Contact Information
25
For this Phase I project, Immobileyes will work
with identified Air Force Stakeholders to evaluate
the feasibility of adapting the company’s HALAR-
Laser solutions to provide high-value c-UAS and c-
drone capabilities in support of United States Air
Force Security Forces (letter of support provided).
Upon successful feasibility demonstration, the
company will work with USAF to develop the
fieldable solution under a Phase II and deploy to
Security Force Squadrons across the globe.
Feasibility of HALAR-Laser Evaluated With These Key Metrics
Immobileyes Contact Information
Atossa Alavi
Chief Executive Officer
atossa@immobileyes.com
330-819-5157
www.Immobileyes.com
Topic: X23.5_CSO 	Proposal Number: FX235-CSO1-0859
“Base-Wide Counter-UAS and Defeat of Drone Surveillance Utilizing Innovative LED-Based Directed Energy System”
Effective: 	obfuscates the optical and/or infrared sensor
systems on common small drone and UAS threats.
Multiplied effect: multiple wavelengths of light ensure
effectiveness against common EO/IR camera systems.
Area effect: solution can be scaled to provide area of effect
operations against swarm UAS systems. Shotgun approach.
Hard to mitigate: Multi-color patterns cannot be defeated
with optical filters on drone cameras.
Scalable and programmable: range, coverage& power can
be tailored to support specific applications or operational
parameters and thresholds.
SWAP-C: 	reduced power lasers allow for significant
reduction in size, weight, power, and cost.', '[{"id":"99f9d800-5ab4-4a13-ba3d-2c0406ac04d3","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"Summary of Project and Contact Information\n25\nFor this Phase I project, Immobileyes will work\nwith identified Air Force Stakeholders to evaluate\nthe feasibility of adapting the company’s HALAR-\nLaser solutions to provide high-value c-UAS and c-\ndrone capabilities in support of United States Air\nForce Security Forces (letter of support provided).\nUpon successful feasibility demonstration, the\ncompany will work with USAF to develop the\nfieldable solution under a Phase II and deploy to\nSecurity Force Squadrons across the globe.\nFeasibility of HALAR-Laser Evaluated With These Key Metrics\nImmobileyes Contact Information\nAtossa Alavi\nChief Executive Officer\natossa@immobileyes.com\n330-819-5157\nwww.Immobileyes.com\nTopic: X23.5_CSO \tProposal Number: FX235-CSO1-0859\n“Base-Wide Counter-UAS and Defeat of Drone Surveillance Utilizing Innovative LED-Based Directed Energy System”\nEffective: \tobfuscates the optical and/or infrared sensor\nsystems on common small drone and UAS threats.\nMultiplied effect: multiple wavelengths of light ensure\neffectiveness against common EO/IR camera systems.\nArea effect: solution can be scaled to provide area of effect\noperations against swarm UAS systems. Shotgun approach.\nHard to mitigate: Multi-color patterns cannot be defeated\nwith optical filters on drone cameras.\nScalable and programmable: range, coverage& power can\nbe tailored to support specific applications or operational\nparameters and thresholds.\nSWAP-C: \treduced power lasers allow for significant\nreduction in size, weight, power, and cost."},"history":[],"provenance":{"source":"imported"},"library_eligible":true}]'::jsonb, NULL, 209, 1541, '{}'::jsonb, 'approved', 0.5, 'pending', 0.5, 0, 'upload', '31c0c32b-a7c5-47fc-817b-55a3b84f960f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, '686842de-ae88-44ac-b724-8e550f079e3e'::uuid, 'tenant', '202