providing a brief description of the effort accomplished. Status Reports: Immobileyes will deliver Status Reports to the TPOC quarterly, starting at month 3, throughout the period of performance of the contract. Technical Interchange Meetings: Immobileyes will establish a series of project Technical Interchange Meetings in support of this project. Based on the availability of our Air Force end-user, these meetings
will be held bi-weekly (or quarterly at a minimum).

Phase II Summary Report: Immobileyes will submit a < 700-word Phase II Summary Report via the TPOC at technical effort completion date that will include a technology description and anticipated
applications/benefits for government/private usage. Additional Reporting: Immobileyes will submit all software documentation, user manuals, engineering drawing, operation and maintenance documentation, updated commercialization results and other related
project documents.
2.2.2.5 Safety Related Deliverables
Immobileyes does not anticipate any requirements for safety related deliverables as the system is not expected
to pose any hazards to the Warfighters. One of the critical aspects of this project will be the characterization
and output of the HALAR-L solution when operated with varying power output, focusing, and steering
parameters achieved during this project. This information will inform the Air Force of any potential EM
safety-related concerns which are not expected.
