  VALUES ('0ca66322-1f52-474d-bcbd-c914c7c2b81c'::uuid, tid, 'primitive', 'p16 · Page 7 of 15
Topic Number: AFX23D-TCSO1 Proposal Numbe', 'Page 7 of 15
Topic Number: AFX23D-TCSO1 Proposal Number: F 2 - 1 7 5 2 8
Proposal Title: “AFSFC Requested Innovative Directed Energy Counter UAS Solution Integrated Into
Proven Detection, Tracking, and Targeting System.”
SBC: Immobileyes
systems, the information provided by the 72d SFS, Air Force Research Laboratory and the Security Forces
Center, the entities most involved in the Air Force C-UAS mission.
2.2.2.2 Task Outline
The major tasks and their associated deliverables are identified below. These tasks were jointly developed by
Immobileyes, Lighthouse, Air Force stakeholders (led by our DAF Customer/End User) and UCF (RI partner).
Task 1: Finalize Requirements Documentation; Design Review; Compile Design Documents
Timeline: Award + 2 months
Summary: Kick-off - Upon award, the Immobileyes Team will meet with customer virtually to conduct an in-
depth requirements analysis, functional use case survey, and operational requirements deep-dive, and to
review/revise the SOW with the TPOC. Each application of the solution will be white boarded from start to
finish and will focus on desired operational functionality; scalability; integration into the Air Force information
technology systems; form/fit/function; and anticipated development/adoption hurdles.
Deliverables: Final Version of Statement of Work; Product Requirements Document; Key Stakeholders
RRAs; Critical Path Document
Task 2: Optical System Design – Laser / Diffractive Beam-Splitters
and Secondary Optics requirements
Timeline: Award + 4 months
Summary: Optical System- Characterization and Design of Gen-1
optical system (laser, diffractive optical element, laser wavelength, pulse
width, aperture size, beamlet number, divergence, pattern requirements,
secondary optics) to meet single drone and swarm defeat requirements. Identification and testing of diffractive
multichannel beam splitter arrays, evaluation of manufacturing process and materials to meet laser power and
wavelengths needed for sensor defeat at range.
Deliverables: Digital Design Files; Software Design Plan; Quarterly Status Report #1.
Task 3: Finalize Designs of Hardware/Software for Integrated Intelligent Counter Drone Solution
Timeline: Award + 6 months
Summary: Integrate with Detection and Tracking: The Immobileyes Team will utilize
the Product Requirements Document accepted in Task 1 to modify existing HALAR-LS
and VCT design files to support development of an integrated stand-alone (but
networkable) intelligent drone swarm detect, define, track, interfere, and defeat solution.
This will include electronic design, case designs, mounting system designs, and peripheral
devices. The completed design files will be locked after acceptance and form the
foundation of the Phase II deliverables. A software strawman architecture that includes
conceptual user interfaces and a data flow diagram will also be developed and delivered.
Deliverables: Digital Design Files; Software Design Plan; Quarterly Status Report #2.
Task 4: Hardware / Software Component Development - Alpha Software Production and Testing
Timeline: Award + 9 months
Summary: Component Development - The Team will source all required components contemplated in the
design files; fabricate the required printed circuit boards (PCBs); integrate the optical element into the laser
system and embed initial operational software for each solution
application specified in the Product Requirements Document. The
Team will manufacture alpha prototypes for the physical and
electronic peripherals required to demonstrate a baseline HALAR-
L/VCT integrated and operational capability. The Immobileyes
Team will deliver an alpha version of a common user and
administrator software package, which will allow for operation and
management of the system. An initial testing plan will be
developed, with support from the Air Force TPOC, for future onsite testing. Initial operational testing success
will be documented and provided.', '[{"id":"89332855-bc71-4fa6-b2a6-1ee855d5660f","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"Page 7 of 15\nTopic Number: AFX23D-TCSO1 Proposal Number: F 2 - 1 7 5 2 8\nProposal Title: “AFSFC Requested Innovative Directed Energy Counter UAS Solution Integrated Into\nProven Detection, Tracking, and Targeting System.”\nSBC: Immobileyes\nsystems, the information provided by the 72d SFS, Air Force Research Laboratory and the Security Forces\nCenter, the entities most involved in the Air Force C-UAS mission.\n2.2.2.2 Task Outline\nThe major tasks and their associated deliverables are identified below. These tasks were jointly developed by\nImmobileyes, Lighthouse, Air Force stakeholders (led by our DAF Customer/End User) and UCF (RI partner).\nTask 1: Finalize Requirements Documentation; Design Review; Compile Design Documents\nTimeline: Award + 2 months\nSummary: Kick-off - Upon award, the Immobileyes Team will meet with customer virtually to conduct an in-\ndepth requirements analysis, functional use case survey, and operational requirements deep-dive, and to\nreview/revise the SOW with the TPOC. Each application of the solution will be white boarded from start to\nfinish and will focus on desired operational functionality; scalability; integration into the Air Force information\ntechnology systems; form/fit/function; and anticipated development/adoption hurdles.\nDeliverables: Final Version of Statement of Work; Product Requirements Document; Key Stakeholders\nRRAs; Critical Path Document\nTask 2: Optical System Design – Laser / Diffractive Beam-Splitters\nand Secondary Optics requirements\nTimeline: Award + 4 months\nSummary: Optical System- Characterization and Design of Gen-1\noptical system (laser, diffractive optical element, laser wavelength, pulse\nwidth, aperture size, beamlet number, divergence, pattern requirements,\nsecondary optics) to meet single drone and swarm defeat requirements. Identification and testing of diffractive\nmultichannel beam splitter arrays, evaluation of manufacturing process and materials to meet laser power and\nwavelengths needed for sensor defeat at range.\nDeliverables: Digital Design Files; Software Design Plan; Quarterly Status Report #1.\nTask 3: Finalize Designs of Hardware/Software for Integrated Intelligent Counter Drone Solution\nTimeline: Award + 6 months\nSummary: Integrate with Detection and Tracking: The Immobileyes Team will utilize\nthe Product Requirements Document accepted in Task 1 to modify existing HALAR-LS\nand VCT design files to support development of an integrated stand-alone (but\nnetworkable) intelligent drone swarm detect, define, track, interfere, and defeat solution.\nThis will include electronic design, case designs, mounting system designs, and peripheral\ndevices. The completed design files will be locked after acceptance and form the\nfoundation of the Phase II deliverables. A software strawman architecture that includes\nconceptual user interfaces and a data flow diagram will also be developed and delivered.\nDeliverables: Digital Design Files; Software Design Plan; Quarterly Status Report #2.\nTask 4: Hardware / Software Component Development - Alpha Software Production and Testing\nTimeline: Award + 9 months\nSummary: Component Development - The Team will source all required components contemplated in the\ndesign files; fabricate the required printed circuit boards (PCBs); integrate the optical element into the laser\nsystem and embed initial operational software for each solution\napplication specified in the Product Requirements Document. The\nTeam will manufacture alpha prototypes for the physical and\nelectronic peripherals required to demonstrate a baseline HALAR-\nL/VCT integrated and operational capability. The Immobileyes\nTeam will deliver an alpha version of a common user and\nadministrator software package, which will allow for operation and\nmanagement of the system. An initial testing plan will be\ndeveloped, with support from the Air Force TPOC, for future onsite testing. Initial operational testing success\nwill be documented and provided."},"history":[],"provenance":{"source":"imported"},"library_eligible":true}]'::jsonb, NULL, 556, 3950, '{}'::jsonb, 'approved', 0.5, 'pending', 0.5, 0, 'upload', 'f0ef96b8-1375-4baf-887d-c6f031ffa9b4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, '686842de-ae88-44ac-b724-8e550f079e3e'::uuid, 'tenant', '2026-08-18T22:42:59.427Z'::timestamptz, '2026-08-18T22:42:59.427Z'::timestamptz, 'admin', uid, '[{"blockIds":["b16"],"sourceAtomId":"6d9d25e2-3aa0-4ab5-b01c-518e4c043627"}]'::jsonb, NULL)
