  VALUES ('d648385d-2556-4307-80cc-ae8d126d1982'::uuid, tid, 'primitive', 'p21 · Page 12 of 15
Topic Number: AFX23D-TCSO1 Proposal Numb', 'Page 12 of 15
Topic Number: AFX23D-TCSO1 Proposal Number: F 2 - 1 7 5 2 8
Proposal Title: “AFSFC Requested Innovative Directed Energy Counter UAS Solution Integrated Into
Proven Detection, Tracking, and Targeting System.”
SBC: Immobileyes
2.3.5 Intellectual Property
Immobileyes owns two broad patents which form the foundation of the
HALAR solutions and multiple patent applications that cover the
security and C-UAS visions of the HALAR technology. Lighthouse
utilizes high-end, commercially available electronics for all components
associated with the Virtual Control Tower. The embedded software
developed by the company and the proprietary video processing and
onboard artificial intelligence is considered Trade Secret and is owned by
the company.
2.3.6 Financing
As outlined in the section below, the Immobileyes team has a set of very supportive venture partners which
include the Entrepreneurs Center, Converge Ventures, the Ohio Gateway Tech Fund, and others who continue
to support the growth of the company with additional venture funding as needed.
Converge Ventures is a Venture Capital support partner for Immobileyes and have
committed to supporting the company’s fund raising, as needed. Letter of support
provided.
The Ohio Gateway Tech Fund is an Ohio based early-stage investment fund committed to
funding innovative and transformative companies from the state. They have committed
$500,000 to Immobileyes for their upcoming capital raise. Letter of support provided.
AlphaMicron is an Ohio-based technology company and strategic partner and investor in
Immobileyes technology. It has provided $350,000 of funds and in-kind contributions and
continues to provide support services to bridge any funding gaps. AlphaMicron has pledged
to mtach future investment efforts Letter of support provided.
2.3.6 Assistance and Mentoring
The Team’s innovative solutions have been funded with millions of dollars funding (internal and external) over
the last several years. Immobileyes has successfully spun out of AlphaMicron, a leading Optics and Liquid
Crystal (LC) R&D and manufacturing facility in Kent, OH and a pioneer of first-in-class flexible LC devices for
the US Army and Air Force. The Immobileyes team enjoys full access to the facilities, equipment, and personnel
of AlphaMicron.
The Ohio PTAC, SBDC, and MEP Programs have been engaged by The Team to
support the commercialization of its technologies. Immobileyes and the partner
companies are well supported by these programs.
The Entrepreneurs’ Center currently includes both Immobileyes and Lighthouse in its
portfolio of Ohio supported companies. EC has considerable experience helping startups
bring their technologies into the military markets (see letter of support).
Derek VanAllen (Subject Matter Expert) – FORTIS A Marine Corps veteran, Derek
brings over 20 years in intelligence and electronic warfare and is a seasoned project
manager and SIGINT expert. His career features 13 overseas deployments, contributing
to his deep understanding of SIGINT, C-UAS, and C-IED operations. He excels in
training and leading teams, briefing high-ranking officials, and developing effective
defense strategies. Holding an active Top Secret/SCI clearance, Derek combines tactical
field experience with strategic acumen.
The Immobileyes Team has extensive experience developing new commercial products and bringing them to
market. This includes expertise in marketing, sales, R&D, engineering support, assembly, fabrication,
manufacturing, and other ideas to market expertise.', '[{"id":"479eca3a-e557-4010-8e9a-8138bb8b0b85","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"Page 12 of 15\nTopic Number: AFX23D-TCSO1 Proposal Number: F 2 - 1 7 5 2 8\nProposal Title: “AFSFC Requested Innovative Directed Energy Counter UAS Solution Integrated Into\nProven Detection, Tracking, and Targeting System.”\nSBC: Immobileyes\n2.3.5 Intellectual Property\nImmobileyes owns two broad patents which form the foundation of the\nHALAR solutions and multiple patent applications that cover the\nsecurity and C-UAS visions of the HALAR technology. Lighthouse\nutilizes high-end, commercially available electronics for all components\nassociated with the Virtual Control Tower. The embedded software\ndeveloped by the company and the proprietary video processing and\nonboard artificial intelligence is considered Trade Secret and is owned by\nthe company.\n2.3.6 Financing\nAs outlined in the section below, the Immobileyes team has a set of very supportive venture partners which\ninclude the Entrepreneurs Center, Converge Ventures, the Ohio Gateway Tech Fund, and others who continue\nto support the growth of the company with additional venture funding as needed.\nConverge Ventures is a Venture Capital support partner for Immobileyes and have\ncommitted to supporting the company’s fund raising, as needed. Letter of support\nprovided.\nThe Ohio Gateway Tech Fund is an Ohio based early-stage investment fund committed to\nfunding innovative and transformative companies from the state. They have committed\n$500,000 to Immobileyes for their upcoming capital raise. Letter of support provided.\nAlphaMicron is an Ohio-based technology company and strategic partner and investor in\nImmobileyes technology. It has provided $350,000 of funds and in-kind contributions and\ncontinues to provide support services to bridge any funding gaps. AlphaMicron has pledged\nto mtach future investment efforts Letter of support provided.\n2.3.6 Assistance and Mentoring\nThe Team’s innovative solutions have been funded with millions of dollars funding (internal and external) over\nthe last several years. Immobileyes has successfully spun out of AlphaMicron, a leading Optics and Liquid\nCrystal (LC) R&D and manufacturing facility in Kent, OH and a pioneer of first-in-class flexible LC devices for\nthe US Army and Air Force. The Immobileyes team enjoys full access to the facilities, equipment, and personnel\nof AlphaMicron.\nThe Ohio PTAC, SBDC, and MEP Programs have been engaged by The Team to\nsupport the commercialization of its technologies. Immobileyes and the partner\ncompanies are well supported by these programs.\nThe Entrepreneurs’ Center currently includes both Immobileyes and Lighthouse in its\nportfolio of Ohio supported companies. EC has considerable experience helping startups\nbring their technologies into the military markets (see letter of support).\nDerek VanAllen (Subject Matter Expert) – FORTIS A Marine Corps veteran, Derek\nbrings over 20 years in intelligence and electronic warfare and is a seasoned project\nmanager and SIGINT expert. His career features 13 overseas deployments, contributing\nto his deep understanding of SIGINT, C-UAS, and C-IED operations. He excels in\ntraining and leading teams, briefing high-ranking officials, and developing effective\ndefense strategies. Holding an active Top Secret/SCI clearance, Derek combines tactical\nfield experience with strategic acumen.\nThe Immobileyes Team has extensive experience developing new commercial products and bringing them to\nmarket. This includes expertise in marketing, sales, R&D, engineering support, assembly, fabrication,\nmanufacturing, and other ideas to market expertise."},"history":[],"provenance":{"source":"imported"},"library_eligible":true}]'::jsonb, NULL, 512, 3544, '{}'::jsonb, 'approved', 0.5, 'pending', 0.5, 0, 'upload', 'f0ef96b8-1375-4baf-887d-c6f031ffa9b4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, '686842de-ae88-44ac-b724-8e550f079e3