  VALUES ('220f7f6f-ec06-4116-b203-ceef9ba70c1a'::uuid, tid, 'primitive', 'p22 · Page 13 of 15
Topic Number: AFX23D-TCSO1 Proposal Numb', 'Page 13 of 15
Topic Number: AFX23D-TCSO1 Proposal Number: F 2 - 1 7 5 2 8
Proposal Title: “AFSFC Requested Innovative Directed Energy Counter UAS Solution Integrated Into
Proven Detection, Tracking, and Targeting System.”
SBC: Immobileyes
2.4 Military Applications and DoD Customers
Small, unmanned aircraft systems (sUAS), commonly called drones, have proliferated rapidly and are
available to nation states and to non-state actors and individuals. These systems could provide U.S. adversaries
with a low-cost means of conducting intelligence, surveillance, and reconnaissance missions against—or
attacking—U.S. forces. Furthermore, many smaller UASs cannot be detected by traditional air defense systems
due to their size, construction material, and flight altitude. As a result, in FY2023, the Department of Defense
(DOD) plans to spend at least $668 million on counter-UAS (C-UAS) research and development and at
least $78 million on C-UAS procurement. The Team is working directly with the Air Force organizations
evaluating emerging C-UAS technologies and were specifically sponsored.
2.5 Foreign Nationals
Immobileyes does not employee non-US citizens and will ensure that any partners also do not.
2.6 Key Personnel
Atossa Alavi, J.D. (Chief Executive Officer) US Citizen - Atossa is an IP attorney
and entrepreneur with 15 years of experience in strategy, management, and
implementation of intellectual property, contracting, team development and
commercialization activities. She specializes in making elite technology available to
the appropriate parties. She holds a law degree (JD) from Case Western Reserve
University and an MPhil. degree in Neuroscience from the University of London.
Bahman Taheri, Ph.D. (Chief Technical Officer) US Citizen Bahman is a liquid
crystal and laser physicist with over 30 years’ experience conducting research for
the Department of Defense and others to understand the effects of lasers on vision.
He is named inventor on over 90 US and International patents. Bahman has
designed and manufactured high-tech electronics which are sold around the world
and are used by the military and commercial consumers. He holds a PhD in physics
from Oklahoma State; Nonlinear Optics and Laser Eye Protection.
Antonio Munoz, Ph.D. (Chief Science Officer) – AlphaMicron - US Citizen An
award-winning scientist with over 30 years of experience in the field of optical
physics, spectroscopy, and lasers, Antonio uses his knowledge of ANSI optics to
characterize device performance of active light management solutions in mission
critical situations. He received his BS, MSc, and Ph.D. in Physics.
Professor. Shin-Tson Wu (RI) - US Citizen - is a Trustee Chair Professor at
CREOL, The UCF College of Optics and Photonics and recipient of multiple
national and international awards in Optics and Excellence in Research. He has co-
authored 7 books, 670 journal papers and 320 conference papers, and obtained 96
issued US patents. His publications have accumulated over 48,000 citations. His lab
specializes in diffractive optics and lightweight, cost effective, LC polymer flat
optics. He received his Ph.D. in Physics from University of Southern California and
BS in Physics from National Taiwan University.
Tyler Bair (Chief Engineer) – Lighthouse - US Citizen - Tyler leads all
development and engineering aspects of the Drone First Responder and Virtual
Control Tower projects at Lighthouse. Tyler was a senior design engineer at
Converge Technologies, where he led the design and commercial development
of noise radars, optical sensing systems, infrared detection systems, autonomous
drone systems, and a litany of other technologies. Tyler has his BS in ECE,
highest honors, from Ohio State.', '[{"id":"7c83aec4-7313-4017-a09a-bc49f63aed68","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"Page 13 of 15\nTopic Number: AFX23D-TCSO1 Proposal Number: F 2 - 1 7 5 2 8\nProposal Title: “AFSFC Requested Innovative Directed Energy Counter UAS Solution Integrated Into\nProven Detection, Tracking, and Targeting System.”\nSBC: Immobileyes\n2.4 Military Applications and DoD Customers\nSmall, unmanned aircraft systems (sUAS), commonly called drones, have proliferated rapidly and are\navailable to nation states and to non-state actors and individuals. These systems could provide U.S. adversaries\nwith a low-cost means of conducting intelligence, surveillance, and reconnaissance missions against—or\nattacking—U.S. forces. Furthermore, many smaller UASs cannot be detected by traditional air defense systems\ndue to their size, construction material, and flight altitude. As a result, in FY2023, the Department of Defense\n(DOD) plans to spend at least $668 million on counter-UAS (C-UAS) research and development and at\nleast $78 million on C-UAS procurement. The Team is working directly with the Air Force organizations\nevaluating emerging C-UAS technologies and were specifically sponsored.\n2.5 Foreign Nationals\nImmobileyes does not employee non-US citizens and will ensure that any partners also do not.\n2.6 Key Personnel\nAtossa Alavi, J.D. (Chief Executive Officer) US Citizen - Atossa is an IP attorney\nand entrepreneur with 15 years of experience in strategy, management, and\nimplementation of intellectual property, contracting, team development and\ncommercialization activities. She specializes in making elite technology available to\nthe appropriate parties. She holds a law degree (JD) from Case Western Reserve\nUniversity and an MPhil. degree in Neuroscience from the University of London.\nBahman Taheri, Ph.D. (Chief Technical Officer) US Citizen Bahman is a liquid\ncrystal and laser physicist with over 30 years’ experience conducting research for\nthe Department of Defense and others to understand the effects of lasers on vision.\nHe is named inventor on over 90 US and International patents. Bahman has\ndesigned and manufactured high-tech electronics which are sold around the world\nand are used by the military and commercial consumers. He holds a PhD in physics\nfrom Oklahoma State; Nonlinear Optics and Laser Eye Protection.\nAntonio Munoz, Ph.D. (Chief Science Officer) – AlphaMicron - US Citizen An\naward-winning scientist with over 30 years of experience in the field of optical\nphysics, spectroscopy, and lasers, Antonio uses his knowledge of ANSI optics to\ncharacterize device performance of active light management solutions in mission\ncritical situations. He received his BS, MSc, and Ph.D. in Physics.\nProfessor. Shin-Tson Wu (RI) - US Citizen - is a Trustee Chair Professor at\nCREOL, The UCF College of Optics and Photonics and recipient of multiple\nnational and international awards in Optics and Excellence in Research. He has co-\nauthored 7 books, 670 journal papers and 320 conference papers, and obtained 96\nissued US patents. His publications have accumulated over 48,000 citations. His lab\nspecializes in diffractive optics and lightweight, cost effective, LC polymer flat\noptics. He received his Ph.D. in Physics from University of Southern California and\nBS in Physics from National Taiwan University.\nTyler Bair (Chief Engineer) – Lighthouse - US Citizen - Tyler leads all\ndevelopment and engineering aspects of the Drone First Responder and Virtual\nControl Tower projects at Lighthouse. Tyler was a senior design engineer at\nConverge Technologies, where he led the design and commercial development\nof noise radars, optical sensing systems, infrared detection systems, autonomous\ndrone systems, and a litany of other technologies. Tyler has his BS in ECE,\nhighest honors, from Ohio State."},"history":[],"provenance":{"source":"imported"},"library_eligible":true}]'::jsonb, NULL, 559, 3724, '{}'::jsonb, 'approved', 0.5, 'pending', 0.5, 0, 'upload', 'f0ef96b8-1375-4baf-887d-c6f031ffa9b4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, '686842de-ae88-44ac-b724-8e550f079e3e'::uuid, 'tenant', '2026-08-18T22:42:59.541Z'::timestamptz, '2026-08-18T22:42:59.541Z'::timestamptz, 'admin', uid, '[{"blockIds":["b22"],"sourceAtomId":"6d9d25e2-3aa0-4ab5-b01c-518e4c043627"}]'::jsonb, NULL)
