STORM employs a graduated, human-in-the-loop optical
response tailored to the threat (Fig. 4). Zone 1
(Warn/Deter) uses low-level visible illumination to
signal presence and encourage compliance. Zone 2
(Dazzle/Disrupt) degrades the drone''s electro-optical
camera, reducing image quality and ISR effectiveness.
Zone 3 (Deny/Damage) concentrates optical energy to
designate targets or disable optical sensors, when
authorized, providing a scalable, non-kinetic response
against EO-guided UAS.
● 	DEXTER™ (Directed-Energy Beam RouTER) is a
low-SWaP adaptive beam-routing architecture developed by
Immobileyes in collaboration with its strategic partner,
AlphaMicron, Inc. (AMI), leveraging AMI''s decades of
expertise in defense-grade liquid crystal (LC) optical devices
for military and aerospace applications. Using adaptive LC
polarization gratings, DEXTER electronically routes, splits,
combines, shapes, and redirects laser energy with no moving
parts. The software-defined optical engine dynamically
switches a single laser beam among multiple output channels,
or combines multiple laser inputs into a single output, in
milliseconds, enabling simultaneous engagement of multiple
drones, rapid beam steering, and scalable swarm defense at
speeds unattainable with conventional mechanically steered optical systems.
● 	Integration: Immobileyes has partnered with PerceptView to provide a mature, sensor-agnostic
integration architecture (Fig. 5). STORM fuses inputs from RF, radar, EO/IR, and other detection
systems and can operate either as a standalone C2 platform or as an integrated effector within existing
Navy and DoW command-and-control architectures, including MEDUSA..
Optical Seeker-Confusion-Overwhelm Mechanism
The effort updates and refines the Navy''s internal research
and development of IR guided seeker-confusion principle
(U.S. Pat. 8,305,252 and 8,212,709). The Navy
demonstrated that a continuous-wave optical source placed
within an imaging seeker''s field of view generates a
localized high-intensity region that the tracking algorithm
interprets as a feature or target; the tracker''s centroid or
