6:45.005Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"75a0e94a-8327-4701-8177-719c05b1db87","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"-- 1 of 7 --"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"b071d695-c833-4917-ac15-b7225a06c756","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"121.702.\n4. Verify that your firm has registered in the SBAS Company Registry at www.sbir.gov by providing the\nSBC Control ID# and uploading the registration confirmation PDF:\nSBC_001832313\nSupporting Documentation:\nSBC_001832313.pdf\t•\n5. It has more than 50% owned by a single Venture Capital Owned Company (VCOC), hedge fund, or\nprivate equity firm\nNO\n6. It has more than 50% owned by multiple business concerns that are VOCs, hedge funds, or private\nequity firms?\nNO\n7. The birth certificates, naturalization papers, or passports show that any individuals it relies upon to\nmeet the eligibility requirements are U.S. citizens or permanent resident aliens in the United States.\nYES\n8. Is 50% or more of your firm owned or managed by a corporate entity? NO\n9. Is your firm affiliated as set forth in 13 CFR Section 121.103? YES\n10. It has met the performance benchmarks as listed by the SBA on their website as eligible to\nparticipate\nYES\n11. Firms PI, CO, or owner, a faculty member or student of an institution of higher education NO\n12. The offeror qualifies as a:\n[ ] Socially and economically disadvantaged SBC\n[X] Women-owned SBC\n[ ] HUBZone-owned SBC\n[ ] Veteran-owned SBC\n[ ] Service Disabled Veteran-owned SBC\n[ ] None Listed\n13. Race of the offeror:\n[ ] American Indian or Alaska Native\n[ ] Native Hawaiian or Other Pacific Islander\n[ ] Asian\n[ ] White\n[ ] Black or African American\n[X] Do not wish to Provide\n14. Ethnicity of the offeror: NON-\nHISPANIC\n15. It is a corporation that has some unpaid Federal tax liability that has been assessed, for which all\njudicial and administrative remedies have not been exhausted or have not lapsed, and that is not being\npaid in a timely manner pursuant to an agreement with the authority responsible for collecting the tax\nliability:\nFALSE\n16. Firm been convicted of a fraud-related crime involving SBIR and/or STTR funds or found civilly liable\nfor a fraud-related violation involving federal funds:\nNO\n17. Firms Principal Investigator (PI) or Corporate Official (CO), or owner been convicted of a fraud-related\ncrime involving SBIR and/or STTR funds or found civilly liable for a fraud-related violation involving federal\nNO"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"d955df6a-f208-4205-914a-ebe721897b9a","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"-- 2 of 7 --"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"9d5b2600-a660-4931-a8af-c127306f2699","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"funds:\nFirm Affiliates:\nName Address Number of Employees\nAlphaMicron Inc. bahman@alphamicron.com\nKent, OH\n34\nSignature:\nPrinted Name Signature Title Business Name Date\nAtossa Alavi Atossa M Alavi CEO Immobileyes Inc. 10/21/2020\nAudit Information\nSummary:\nHas your Firm ever had a DCAA review?NO\nVOL I - Proposal Summary\nSummary:\nProposed Base Duration (in months): 6\nOption 1 Duration (in months): 6\nTechnical Abstract:\nFirst-person-view (FPV) fiber-optic visual-navigation enabled drones present an urgent operational challenge on the modern\nbattlefield. Unconstrained by radiofrequency (RF) links, immune to RF jamming, and operating without GPS, these\nplatforms rely on continuous electro-optical (EO) imagery for terminal guidance. Current counter-UAS (C-UAS)\nsystems—optimized for RF disruption, GPS spoofing, or costly kinetic interceptors—fail to provide a cost-effective\noperationally sound defense against swarms of low-cost, fiber-guided threats targeting ships, installations, and the Navy''s\nexpeditionary forces.\nFor this effort, Immobileyes proposes Guided Hostile Optical Sensor-hijacking (GHOST), an innovative software-definable\nnon-kinetic countermeasure architecture integrating two core technologies: STORM™ (Smart Tracking &amp; Optical\nResponse Mitigation) and DEXTER™ (Directed-Energy Beam RouTER). STORM incorporates Modular Open Systems"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"af421c2e-ed3a-4894-946f-c7cb8ffb3c58","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"-- 3 of 7 --"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"364b19e2-90f7-4713-ace6-5f0dea64602c","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"Approach (MOSA) sensor-agnostic cueing (EO/IR, radar, RF) to deliver a graduated response: Zone 1 (Warn/Deter), Zone 2\n(Dazzle/Disrupt), and Zone 3 (Deny/Damage). DEXTER, developed in partnership with AlphaMicron, uses solid-state liquid\ncrystal (LC) polarization gratings to electronically route, split, and steer a sub-kilowatt laser beam into single- or multi-beam\nconfigurations in milliseconds with no moving parts and at a very low manufacture price at scale.\nGHOST adapts and extends proven optical seeker-confusion concepts, previously research, developed, and\npatented by the Navy, to uncooled EO camera sensors typical on almost all modern drones. By projecting well\ncontrolled multi-wavelength dynamic-power optical energy into an incoming drone’s sensor field of view, the system\ninduces localized saturation, image blooming, contrast collapse, and false high-intensity features. This disrupts feature-\ntracking algorithms and optical-flow guidance, breaking terminal lock and misguiding the drone without requiring\nphysical destruction.\nThe Phase I effort establishes technical feasibility by modeling and measuring DEXTER''s laser-induced optical\nperturbations across representative FPV/EO cameras, defining the software/hardware architecture for Navy MOSA\nintegration, and quantifying performance gains over mechanically steered systems. The Phase I Option develops a closed-\nloop laboratory breadboard tracking demonstration and a maritime platform integration plan. GHOST delivers a low-\nSWaP, non-kinetic capability to defeat RF-jamming-resistant, EO-guided drones, solving magazine-depth and cost-exchange\nchallenges for USN and USMC assets.\nThe Immobileyes team proposed is comprised of industry leading LCD reserchers holding over 90 patents in the field as\nwell as recognized experts in fully integrated end-to-end counter UAS solutions currently fielded across the DoW. The\ninnovative nature of DEXTER provides the Navy with a low-cost, highly scalable, first-of-its-kind non-kinetic drone defeat\nsolution.\nAnticipated Benefits/Potential Commercial Applications of the Research or Development:\nNaval Special Warfare & Tactical Maritime Operations:\nGHOST delivers a crucial, low Size, Weight, Power, and Cost (SWaP-C) non-kinetic countermeasure specifically engineered to\nprotect Navy SEALs, Special Boat Teams, and tactical craft (e.g., Combatant Craft Assault, RHIBs) against fiber-\noptic, EO-guided FPV drones. Because fiber-guided and visual-navigation drones operate without RF emissions or GPS\ndependencies, legacy electronic warfare jammers fail. By integrating DEXTER’s solid-state liquid-crystal beam router (no\nmoving parts) onto tactical boats or light vehicles, special operations personnel gain immediate, millisecond-level\noptical disruption without the space, power, weight, or cooling penalties of conventional high-power lasers or\nheavy gimbals. The non-kinetic, graduated response framework (Warn, Dazzle, Deny) preserves tactical stealth and minimizes\ncollateral risk during covert littoral ingress and coastal maneuvers.\nShipboard & Naval Base Point Defense:"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"ed76a3e8-78bd-499c-b072-fb3f6a7061b3","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"-- 4 of 7 --"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"2f062a9a-ff41-4f89-91a2-53b258bb9c30","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"For NAVSEA and NAVAIR, GHOST directly addresses an urgent capability gap in protecting surface combatants, littoral\nvessels, flight lines, munitions magazines, and naval installations against cheap, saturating swarm attacks.\nTraditional kinetic interceptors create severe magazine-depth limitations and unfavorable cost-exchange imbalances when\nexpending high-cost munitions against sub-$1,000 airframes. GHOST electronically splits a single continuous-wave laser into\ndynamic multi-beam arrays, enabling one effector to misguide multiple incoming EO-guided drones simultaneously without\nmechanical lag. Open MOSA interfaces allow seamless integration into existing Navy command-and-control and\nsensor networks (EO/IR, radar, RF), expanding defensive perimeters well beyond base fence lines.\nCross-Service & High-Value Asset (HVA) Protection:\nThe software-defined architecture naturally scales to aggressively protect high-value military and government assets across\nthe Joint Force. Primary transition targets include USMC expeditionary units, Army mobile air defense (RCCTO), Air\nForce Security Forces (building on an established TRL-5 Tinker AFB baseline), and Homeland Security partners\n(DHS, DOJ, Coast Guard) tasked with proactively protecting critical national infrastructure, nuclear facilities, federal\ncompounds, deep-water ports, and border checkpoints under updated interagency C-UAS guidance.\nCommercial & Dual-Use Applications:\nBeyond defense, GHOST provides non-disruptive, FAA-aware optical mitigation where kinetic force or RF jamming is\nlegally restricted, dangerous, or causes unacceptable spectrum interference. Commercial markets include commercial\nairports, civilian flight corridors, maritime terminals, national energy grids, and large public venues. Commercialization will\nstrongly leverage established liquid-crystal manufacturing lines, regional defense innovation hubs, and strategic\nindustry partnerships, ensuring a scalable domestic supply chain.\nAttention:\nDisclaimer: For any purpose other than to evaluate the proposal, this data except proposal cover sheets shall not\nbe disclosed outside the Government and shall not be duplicated, used or disclosed in whole or in part, provided\nthat if a contract is awarded to this proposer as a result of or in connection with the submission of this data, the\nGovernment shall have the right to duplicate, use or disclose the data to the extent provided in the funding\nagreement. This restriction does not limit the Government''s right to use information contained in the data if it is\nobtained from another source without restriction. This restriction does not apply to routine handling of proposals\nfor administrative purposes by Government support contractors. The data subject to this restriction is contained\non the pages of the proposal listed on the line below.\nAddition:\nEnter the page numbers separated by a space of the pages in the proposal that are considered proprietary:\nList a maximum of 8 Key Words or phrases, separated by commas, that describe the Project:\nCUAS, Counter UAS, Laser, Dazzle, Mobile, Non-Kinetic, Directed Energy, Swarm Defeat"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"a67baccd-f768-449b-860b-6c3c8abe5cd1","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"-- 5 of 7 --"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"0f6d060c-af73-42a2-8136-601e4e1179ce","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"VOL I - Proposal Certification\nSummary:"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"ee79a52f-f81e-44d1-b251-7f6f295cf191","type":"numbered_list","style":{},"content":{"items":[{"text":"At a minimum, two thirds of the work in Phase I will be carried out by your small business as defined by 13 C.F.R"}]},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"p