17. Does your firm allow for the release of its contact information to Economic Development Organizations? YES', '[{"id":"2f062a9a-ff41-4f89-91a2-53b258bb9c30","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"For NAVSEA and NAVAIR, GHOST directly addresses an urgent capability gap in protecting surface combatants, littoral\nvessels, flight lines, munitions magazines, and naval installations against cheap, saturating swarm attacks.\nTraditional kinetic interceptors create severe magazine-depth limitations and unfavorable cost-exchange imbalances when\nexpending high-cost munitions against sub-$1,000 airframes. GHOST electronically splits a single continuous-wave laser into\ndynamic multi-beam arrays, enabling one effector to misguide multiple incoming EO-guided drones simultaneously without\nmechanical lag. Open MOSA interfaces allow seamless integration into existing Navy command-and-control and\nsensor networks (EO/IR, radar, RF), expanding defensive perimeters well beyond base fence lines.\nCross-Service & High-Value Asset (HVA) Protection:\nThe software-defined architecture naturally scales to aggressively protect high-value military and government assets across\nthe Joint Force. Primary transition targets include USMC expeditionary units, Army mobile air defense (RCCTO), Air\nForce Security Forces (building on an established TRL-5 Tinker AFB baseline), and Homeland Security partners\n(DHS, DOJ, Coast Guard) tasked with proactively protecting critical national infrastructure, nuclear facilities, federal\ncompounds, deep-water ports, and border checkpoints under updated interagency C-UAS guidance.\nCommercial & Dual-Use Applications:\nBeyond defense, GHOST provides non-disruptive, FAA-aware optical mitigation where kinetic force or RF jamming is\nlegally restricted, dangerous, or causes unacceptable spectrum interference. Commercial markets include commercial\nairports, civilian flight corridors, maritime terminals, national energy grids, and large public venues. Commercialization will\nstrongly leverage established liquid-crystal manufacturing lines, regional defense innovation hubs, and strategic\nindustry partnerships, ensuring a scalable domestic supply chain.\nAttention:\nDisclaimer: For any purpose other than to evaluate the proposal, this data except proposal cover sheets shall not\nbe disclosed outside the Government and shall not be duplicated, used or disclosed in whole or in part, provided\nthat if a contract is awarded to this proposer as a result of or in connection with the submission of this data, the\nGovernment shall have the right to duplicate, use or disclose the data to the extent provided in the funding\nagreement. This restriction does not limit the Government''s right to use information contained in the data if it is\nobtained from another source without restriction. This restriction does not apply to routine handling of proposals\nfor administrative purposes by Government support contractors. The data subject to this restriction is contained\non the pages of the proposal listed on the line below.\nAddition:\nEnter the page numbers separated by a space of the pages in the proposal that are considered proprietary:\nList a maximum of 8 Key Words or phrases, separated by commas, that describe the Project:\nCUAS, Counter UAS, Laser, Dazzle, Mobile, Non-Kinetic, Directed Energy, Swarm Defeat"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"a67baccd-f768-449b-860b-6c3c8abe5cd1","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"-- 5 of 7 --"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"0f6d060c-af73-42a2-8136-601e4e1179ce","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"VOL I - Proposal Certification\nSummary:"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"ee79a52f-f81e-44d1-b251-7f6f295cf191","type":"numbered_list","style":{},"content":{"items":[{"text":"At a minimum, two thirds of the work in Phase I will be carried out by your small business as defined by 13 C.F.R"}]},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"6de1e48f-ae12-493e-a0cb-708ca770603e","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"Section 701-705. The numbers for this certification are derived from the budget template. To update these\nnumbers, review and revise your budget data. If the minimum percentage of work numbers are not met, then a\nletter of explanation or written approval from the funding officer is required.\nPlease note that some components will not accept any deviation from the Percentage of Work (POW) minimum\nrequirements. Please check your component instructions regarding the POW requirements.\nYES\nFirm POW 100%\nSubcontractor POW 0%\n2. Is primary employment of the principal investigator with your firm as defined by 13 C.F.R Section 701-705? YES\n3. During the performance of the contract, the research and development will be performed in the\nUnited States?\nYES\n4. During the performance of the contract, the research and development will be performed at the\nofferors facilities by the offerors employees except as otherwise indicated in the technical\nproposal?\nYES\n5. Do you plan to use Federal facilities, laboratories, or equipment? NO\n6. The offeror understands and shall comply with export control regulations. YES\n7. There will be ITAR/EAR data in this work and/or deliverables. YES\n8. Has a proposal for essentially equivalent work been submitted to other US government agencies or DoD\ncomponents?\nNO\n9. Has a contract been awarded for any of the proposals listed above? NO\n10. Firm will notify the Federal agency immediately if all or a portion of the work authorized and funded\nunder this proposal is subsequently funded by another Federal agency?\nYES\n11. Are you submitting assertions in accordance with DFARS 252.227-7017 Identification and assertions use,\nrelease, or disclosure restriction?\nNO\n12. Are you proposing research that utilizes human/animal subjects or a recombinant DNA as described in DoDI\n3216.01, 32 C.F.R. Section 219, and National Institutes of Health Guidelines for Research Involving Recombinant DNA\nof the solicitation?\nNO\n13. Are teaming partners or subcontractors proposed? NO\n14. Are you proposing to use foreign nationals as defined in 22 CFR 120.16 for work under the proposed effort? NO\n15. What percentage of the principal investigators total time will be on the project? 25%\n16. Is the principal investigator socially/economically disadvantaged? NO\n17. Does your firm allow for the release of its contact information to Economic Development Organizations? YES"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-18T22:46:45.005Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true}]'::jsonb, NULL, 833, 5691, '{}'::jsonb, 'approved', 0.5, 'pending', 0.5, 0, 'upload', '684d8917-6a86-4eeb-806d-4db1cd3a655f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, '686842de-ae88-44ac-b724-8e550f079e3e'::uuid, 'tenant', '2026-08-18T22:46:45.060Z'::timestamptz, '2026-08-18T22:46:45.060Z'::timestamptz, 'admin', uid, '[{"blockIds":["b2"],"sourceAtom